{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Darling I have [C]come to tell [G]you
[G]Though it almost breaks my [D]heart
[G]But before the [C]morning [G]darling
[D]We'll be many miles [G]apart
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Don't this road look rough and [G]rocky
[G]Don't that sea look wide and [D]deep
[G]Don't my baby [C]look the [G]sweetest
[D]When she's in my arms [G]asleep[D][G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Can't you hear the night birds crying
Far across the deep blue sea
While of those others you are thinking
Won't you sometimes think of me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
One more kiss before I leave you
One more kiss before we part
You have caused me lots of trouble
Darling you have broke my heart
{end_of_chorus}
